# Kubernetes Lab: Create an Nginx Pod

## 📌 Objective

Create a Kubernetes pod with the following specifications:

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Pod Name | `pod-nginx` |
| Image | `nginx:latest` |
| Container Name | `nginx-container` |
| Label | `app=nginx_app` |

> **Note:** The Kubernetes cluster is already configured on the jump host, so `kubectl` can be used directly.

---

# Lab Environment

| Component | Details |
|-----------|---------|
| Platform | Kubernetes |
| Tool | kubectl |
| Cluster Access | Pre-configured on Jump Host |

---

# Solution

## Step 1: Verify Cluster Connectivity

```bash
kubectl cluster-info
```

Expected output:

```text
Kubernetes control plane is running...
CoreDNS is running...
```

---

## Step 2: Create the Pod

```bash
kubectl run pod-nginx \
  --image=nginx:latest \
  --labels=app=nginx_app \
  --restart=Never \
  --overrides='{
    "spec":{
      "containers":[
        {
          "name":"nginx-container",
          "image":"nginx:latest"
        }
      ]
    }
  }'
```

---

## Step 3: Verify the Pod

```bash
kubectl get pods
```

Example output:

```text
NAME         READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE
pod-nginx    1/1     Running   0          15s
```

---

## Step 4: Verify Labels

```bash
kubectl get pod pod-nginx --show-labels
```

Expected:

```text
NAME         READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE   LABELS
pod-nginx    1/1     Running   0          20s   app=nginx_app
```

---

## Step 5: Verify Container Name

```bash
kubectl describe pod pod-nginx
```

Container section:

```text
Containers:
  nginx-container:
    Image: nginx:latest
```

---

# Alternative YAML Manifest

Create a file named `pod-nginx.yaml`

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: pod-nginx
  labels:
    app: nginx_app

spec:
  containers:
    - name: nginx-container
      image: nginx:latest
```

Deploy the pod:

```bash
kubectl apply -f pod-nginx.yaml
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl get pods
```

---

# Validation Commands

Check pod:

```bash
kubectl get pod pod-nginx
```

Check labels:

```bash
kubectl get pod pod-nginx --show-labels
```

Check image:

```bash
kubectl get pod pod-nginx -o jsonpath='{.spec.containers[0].image}'
```

Output:

```text
nginx:latest
```

Check container name:

```bash
kubectl get pod pod-nginx -o jsonpath='{.spec.containers[0].name}'
```

Output:

```text
nginx-container
```

